Plugin for ACE CPC Emulator which provides GX4000/Plus analog
joystick support, based on the Tennis Cup 2 cartridge's analog
joystick routine:

  https://www.cpcwiki.eu/index.php/Tennis_Cup_2_(cartridge)

The ADC returns values 00h-3Fh (0-63). Center position is 1Fh (31).
Directions are determined via the Tennis Cup 2 algorithm:
  - Deflection >= +14h from center = right or down
  - Deflection <= -15h from center = left or up
  - Dead zone of +/-13h around center

Installation:
-------------
Copy the content of the archive to your ACE drawer.
Use the ACE-Analog icon to launch ACE with Analog support enabled.

Settings:
---------
The plugin settings panel lets you select the joystick port:
  - Joystick Port 0: Analog on joystick port A
  - Joystick Port 1: Analog on joystick port B (default)

Usage:
------
The GX4000/Plus ADC provides two channels for X/Y position.
The included Z80 driver (driver/analog_driver.asm) reads the ADC
and converts analog values to digital directions, with fire button
read from digital joystick 1.

Files:
------
  Plugins/analog.acepansion   - The ACEpansion plugin binary
  Help/analog.acepansion.guide - Documentation (English)
  driver/analog_driver.asm     - Z80 assembly driver source
  driver/analog_demo.bas       - BASIC demonstration program

More information:
  https://www.cpcwiki.eu/index.php/Tennis_Cup_2_(cartridge)
